<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <%- include('partials/head') %>
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/legal-contact.css">
</head>

<body>
    <%- include('partials/header') %>
        <%- include('partials/flash') %>

            <main class="page-wrapper">
                <!-- HOTSTAR-STYLE HERO BANNER -->
                <section class="legal-hero-card">
                    <div class="legal-hero-backdrop"></div>
                    <div class="legal-overlay-left"></div>
                    <div class="legal-overlay-bottom"></div>

                    <div class="legal-hero-content">
                        <div class="hero-tags">
                            <span class="hotstar-pill secure-pill">
                                <i class="fa-solid fa-file-contract"></i> CODE OF CONDUCT
                            </span>
                            <span class="hotstar-pill status-pill">
                                <span class="pulsing-dot"></span> ENFORCED ACROSS ALL PLATFORMS
                            </span>
                        </div>

                        <h1 class="glitch-title" data-text="TERMS & CONDITIONS">
                            TERMS & <span class="gold-text">CONDITIONS</span>
                        </h1>

                        <p class="hero-subtitle">
                            Standard community charter, tournament fair play regulations, and member responsibilities
                            within the ATX ecosystem.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <!-- TERMS DOCUMENT CONTAINER -->
                <section class="cyber-card content-card">
                    <div class="hud-corner tl"></div>
                    <div class="hud-corner br"></div>

                    <div class="legal-body">
                        <p class="lead-text">
                            By accessing, logging into, or participating in the <strong>ATX Family</strong> web portal,
                            Discord server, or official tournament events, you agree to adhere to the following Terms of
                            Service.
                        </p>

                        <div class="policy-block">
                            <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-scale-balanced gold-text"></i> 1. Community Conduct & Respect</h2>
                            <p>
                                ATX is built on loyalty, camaraderie, and mutual respect. Harassment, hate speech,
                                disruptive trolling, or targeted toxicity directed toward members or administrative
                                staff will result in an immediate and non-negotiable community ban.
                            </p>
                        </div>

                        <div class="policy-block">
                            <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-trophy gold-text"></i> 2. Fair Play & Competitive Integrity</h2>
                            <p>
                                Participation in ATX tournaments, trivia gauntlets, and Werewolf matches demands strict
                                integrity. Screen cheating, alt account abuse, exploit automation, or timer manipulation
                                will result in disqualification and tournament blacklisting.
                            </p>
                        </div>

                        <div class="policy-block">
                            <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-id-badge gold-text"></i> 3. Account Responsibility & Media Uploads
                            </h2>
                            <p>
                                You are responsible for all actions taken under your authenticated account. Custom
                                profile avatars must not contain illegal, sexually explicit, graphic, or
                                copyright-infringing imagery.
                            </p>
                        </div>

                        <div class="policy-block">
                            <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-shield-halved gold-text"></i> 4. Administration Authority</h2>
                            <p>
                                The ATX Family platform is provided on an "as is" basis. Staff reserves final authority
                                to adjust leaderboard points, arbitrate disputed matches, update platform features, and
                                revoke access for violations of server policy.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>
            </main>

            <%- include('partials/footer') %>
</body>

</html>